WEBVTT

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.490
Welcome to CareConsent.

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:07.100
This course follows everyday hospital
work, from registration and patient

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:12.975
choices through privacy requests,
administration and incident response.

00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:17.715
We use CareConsent Training Hospital and
invented people throughout.

00:00:17.715 --> 00:00:20.970
Pause whenever you need time to practise.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:25.780
Some chapters explain restricted
administrator or technical workflows;

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:30.880
follow only the chapters appropriate to
your account and responsibilities.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.610
Keep this course beside your practice
workspace.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:41.315
Before entering anything, look for Public
synthetic demo or the development warning.

00:00:41.315 --> 00:00:46.295
These screens are for practice, not real
patient registration.

00:00:46.295 --> 00:00:52.110
All names, hospital numbers and contact
references shown here are invented.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:57.645
The SMS simulator displays a test code and
sends no text message.

00:00:57.645 --> 00:01:02.175
A green success message in training does
not establish a production deployment,

00:01:02.175 --> 00:01:06.446
legal approval or communication with
another organisation.

00:01:07.193 --> 00:01:11.883
Legal references were checked on
twenty-seven October twenty twenty-six:

00:01:11.883 --> 00:01:16.603
the twenty twenty-three Digital Personal
Data Protection Act, final twenty

00:01:16.603 --> 00:01:22.628
twenty-five Rules, December corrigendum
and October twenty twenty-six Order.

00:01:22.628 --> 00:01:27.498
Commencement is phased; not every duty is
already effective.

00:01:27.498 --> 00:01:31.128
The seventy-two-hour detailed
breach-report rule applies when its

00:01:31.128 --> 00:01:33.298
provisions commence.

00:01:33.298 --> 00:01:37.898
The demo’s forty-eight-hour retention
notice is a configured guardrail, not a

00:01:37.898 --> 00:01:40.798
blanket hospital obligation.

00:01:40.798 --> 00:01:46.058
Read References and Scope, confirm the
applicable phase, and obtain hospital

00:01:46.058 --> 00:01:50.623
approval and production qualification
before real patient use.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.595
Different accounts see different
navigation.

00:01:54.595 --> 00:02:00.375
Reception can work with assigned patients;
clinicians have clinical responsibilities;

00:02:00.375 --> 00:02:06.160
privacy officers handle privacy cases;
auditors inspect evidence.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:10.130
A hospital administrator manages
configuration and accounts without

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:13.930
automatically receiving patient-record
access.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:18.445
If a page or button is absent, first check
your role.

00:02:18.445 --> 00:02:22.620
Do not borrow a colleague's account or
change a web address to reach restricted

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.281
information.

00:02:25.027 --> 00:02:30.752
CareConsent records choices about personal
information for specific purposes.

00:02:30.752 --> 00:02:36.202
It also has a separate register for
references to clinical procedure evidence.

00:02:36.202 --> 00:02:41.222
Neither registration, an OTP nor a
downloaded data receipt signs a surgery

00:02:41.222 --> 00:02:43.132
consent form.

00:02:43.132 --> 00:02:48.342
Clinicians must still complete their
approved procedure-specific process.

00:02:48.342 --> 00:02:53.237
A patient's refusal of optional hospital
offers must not be treated as refusal of

00:02:53.237 --> 00:02:57.108
care or authority to ignore emergency
procedures.

00:02:57.818 --> 00:03:03.093
At Welcome back, choose CareConsent
Training Hospital in Hospital.

00:03:03.093 --> 00:03:08.203
Enter the Work email and Password provided
for your training role, then select Open

00:03:08.203 --> 00:03:09.953
workspace.

00:03:09.953 --> 00:03:12.948
Read any error before trying again.

00:03:12.948 --> 00:03:17.133
A patient uses a separately provisioned
patient account.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:22.178
A consent verification code from reception
is not a workspace password and cannot be

00:03:22.178 --> 00:03:25.244
used to open somebody's patient portal.

00:03:25.985 --> 00:03:30.660
If an Authenticator code is requested,
obtain the current code from your own

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:34.055
authenticator app and choose Confirm code.

00:03:34.055 --> 00:03:40.085
For initial enrolment, follow Set up an
authenticator and Confirm authenticator.

00:03:40.085 --> 00:03:46.410
Inside Readiness & settings, Two-step
sign-in also offers Set up authenticator.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:50.235
Save recovery codes privately when they
appear.

00:03:50.235 --> 00:03:55.070
Training screenshots must never be used as
genuine authenticator keys or recovery

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:56.605
material.

00:03:57.318 --> 00:04:01.953
If the authenticator device is
unavailable, choose Use a recovery code at

00:04:01.953 --> 00:04:05.573
the sign-in challenge and enter one unused
code.

00:04:05.573 --> 00:04:08.628
Each recovery code works once.

00:04:08.628 --> 00:04:12.098
Repeated failed attempts can lock the
account.

00:04:12.098 --> 00:04:17.293
Stop guessing and contact the authorised
administrator, who can investigate and use

00:04:17.293 --> 00:04:20.158
Unlock or Reset authenticator.

00:04:20.158 --> 00:04:24.668
A forgotten password has an
administrator-managed process; this build

00:04:24.668 --> 00:04:28.924
does not offer a patient phone-only
recovery shortcut.

00:04:29.652 --> 00:04:34.342
Open Readiness & settings and find Your
workspace preferences.

00:04:34.342 --> 00:04:40.617
Language changes the interface between
English, Tamil, Telugu and Hindi.

00:04:40.617 --> 00:04:44.267
Appearance offers System, Light and Dark.

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:49.927
Text size offers Standard, Large and Extra
large, with a separate High contrast

00:04:49.927 --> 00:04:51.367
option.

00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:54.137
These are display preferences.

00:04:54.137 --> 00:04:58.717
Changing them does not translate an old
receipt or change the patient's recorded

00:04:58.717 --> 00:05:00.638
notice language.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:07.000
On Review patient choices, read the notice
in the patient's selected language.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.360
Listen to notice uses an available
matching on-device voice.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:15.695
Pause, Resume and Stop reading control
playback.

00:05:15.695 --> 00:05:20.980
If the matching voice is unavailable, the
app explains that limitation; use the

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:25.145
written transcript or approved
communication assistance.

00:05:25.145 --> 00:05:29.795
Listening is optional and is never counted
as consent by itself.

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:32.986
Patient identifiers are not spoken.

00:05:33.735 --> 00:05:39.035
Keyboard users can move with Tab and
activate controls with Enter or Space.

00:05:39.035 --> 00:05:41.990
Use Skip to workspace when offered.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:46.800
On smaller screens, Open navigation
reveals the menu.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:50.425
Increase text size before struggling to
read.

00:05:50.425 --> 00:05:54.340
Offer communication support chosen by the
patient.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:59.150
Disability alone does not remove the
person's ability to decide, and an audio

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:03.921
button does not establish that every
accessibility need has been met.

00:06:04.652 --> 00:06:08.137
Select Overview to open Consent overview.

00:06:08.137 --> 00:06:12.262
Registered patients counts records in your
permitted scope.

00:06:12.262 --> 00:06:17.217
Patients with consent means at least one
active purpose, not permission for every

00:06:17.217 --> 00:06:18.832
purpose.

00:06:18.832 --> 00:06:23.417
Awaiting consent indicates no recorded
consent in that summary.

00:06:23.417 --> 00:06:27.817
Withdrawn purposes counts individual
purpose withdrawals.

00:06:27.817 --> 00:06:32.427
Read the explanatory labels before
comparing numbers, and remember that your

00:06:32.427 --> 00:06:35.598
role and branch influence what you can
see.

00:06:36.318 --> 00:06:41.318
Look at Needs your attention for privacy
requests and integration work.

00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:47.058
A service target is a date for follow-up,
not proof that a response was sent.

00:06:47.058 --> 00:06:51.183
Pending integration events need
investigation even when local consent was

00:06:51.183 --> 00:06:52.623
saved.

00:06:52.623 --> 00:06:56.478
Use View all patients to continue with the
directory.

00:06:56.478 --> 00:07:01.083
Follow the hospital's escalation process
for overdue requests rather than simply

00:07:01.083 --> 00:07:03.824
closing them to clear the dashboard.

00:07:04.568 --> 00:07:08.573
Open Patient directory and select Register
patient.

00:07:08.573 --> 00:07:13.278
In Register a patient, enter Training
Adult Patient under Full name and a unique

00:07:13.278 --> 00:07:15.698
training Hospital number.

00:07:15.698 --> 00:07:20.208
Enter the agreed synthetic date of birth
and training Mobile number, using ten

00:07:20.208 --> 00:07:23.073
digits without plus ninety-one.

00:07:23.073 --> 00:07:25.708
Select the correct Department.

00:07:25.708 --> 00:07:30.708
Check the identity against your training
exercise before continuing; a duplicate

00:07:30.708 --> 00:07:34.849
hospital number should be investigated
rather than bypassed.

00:07:35.568 --> 00:07:39.943
Set Patient notice language to the
language the patient understands,

00:07:39.943 --> 00:07:43.388
independently of your interface
preference.

00:07:43.388 --> 00:07:48.388
For this adult exercise, leave guardian
details unused.

00:07:48.388 --> 00:07:53.078
Review every field, then select Save and
review choices.

00:07:53.078 --> 00:07:57.878
Wait for the saved record or the next
screen before assuming success.

00:07:57.878 --> 00:08:02.588
If validation identifies a mistake,
correct that field.

00:08:02.588 --> 00:08:06.553
Do not invent a guardian or another
person's phone number just to complete

00:08:06.553 --> 00:08:08.283
registration.

00:08:09.027 --> 00:08:13.947
The Review patient choices screen shows
the notice version and language.

00:08:13.947 --> 00:08:18.407
Read Privacy notice and the hospital's
published contact and request channels

00:08:18.407 --> 00:08:20.132
where present.

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:24.177
In training, a draft warning may remain
visible.

00:08:24.177 --> 00:08:29.107
In real operation, staff must use the
approved effective publication for that

00:08:29.107 --> 00:08:30.722
language.

00:08:30.722 --> 00:08:35.907
An unavailable notice is a stop condition
for this consent workflow, not a reason to

00:08:35.907 --> 00:08:38.527
silently switch languages.

00:08:39.277 --> 00:08:43.907
Under Choose each purpose separately,
explain each purpose's Data and Use

00:08:43.907 --> 00:08:45.707
descriptions.

00:08:45.707 --> 00:08:51.077
Insurance claim processing does not
automatically approve every recipient.

00:08:51.077 --> 00:08:56.497
Research contact means contact about a
study, not study participation or release

00:08:56.497 --> 00:08:58.692
of research records.

00:08:58.692 --> 00:09:01.902
Hospital news and offers is optional.

00:09:01.902 --> 00:09:06.587
Select only the patient's agreed purposes,
then ask them to make the displayed

00:09:06.587 --> 00:09:08.452
confirmation.

00:09:08.452 --> 00:09:11.537
Do not preselect choices for speed.

00:09:12.277 --> 00:09:17.087
If the patient does not agree, choose
Close without consent.

00:09:17.087 --> 00:09:20.572
No new purpose is granted through this
action.

00:09:20.572 --> 00:09:26.327
Importantly, leaving a box unticked does
not withdraw a purpose granted previously;

00:09:26.327 --> 00:09:29.512
use the separate Withdraw action for that.

00:09:29.512 --> 00:09:33.167
This screen is not a complete
refusal-of-treatment process or an

00:09:33.167 --> 00:09:35.717
emergency decision tool.

00:09:35.717 --> 00:09:39.322
Escalate care questions through the
hospital's approved clinical and

00:09:39.322 --> 00:09:41.883
lawful-basis procedures.

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:48.995
After the patient confirms the selected
purposes, choose Generate simulated OTP.

00:09:48.995 --> 00:09:54.845
The next screen says SMS simulator — no
message sent and displays Test code.

00:09:54.845 --> 00:10:01.660
Enter that six-digit code in Verification
code, then select Verify & record consent.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:06.830
In a qualified live setup, the button and
delivery process differ.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:11.700
Never tell a patient that a training test
code arrived by SMS.

00:10:12.443 --> 00:10:15.608
Read any verification error carefully.

00:10:15.608 --> 00:10:20.703
Codes expire after five minutes and allow
a limited number of attempts.

00:10:20.703 --> 00:10:25.613
For an incorrect training code, correct
the entry instead of repeatedly submitting

00:10:25.613 --> 00:10:27.163
guesses.

00:10:27.163 --> 00:10:32.043
Use Change choices if the selected
purposes need changing, then obtain a new

00:10:32.043 --> 00:10:33.643
challenge.

00:10:33.643 --> 00:10:38.173
A code for an earlier notice or different
purposes must not be reused for the new

00:10:38.173 --> 00:10:39.583
choice.

00:10:40.318 --> 00:10:45.498
A network timeout may happen after a
server has accepted an operation.

00:10:45.498 --> 00:10:50.368
If the screen offers Retry the same
operation, keep the same request intact

00:10:50.368 --> 00:10:53.043
and use that recovery action.

00:10:53.043 --> 00:10:57.248
Avoid double-clicking, changing the form
and treating a retry as a new

00:10:57.248 --> 00:10:59.088
registration.

00:10:59.088 --> 00:11:04.303
Refresh the authorised patient view to
reconcile the result when instructed.

00:11:04.303 --> 00:11:09.478
If the outcome remains unclear, contact
support before recording contradictory

00:11:09.478 --> 00:11:11.013
choices.

00:11:11.735 --> 00:11:16.945
After verification, return to Patient
consent profile and find Signed consent

00:11:16.945 --> 00:11:18.565
receipts.

00:11:18.565 --> 00:11:24.975
Choose Download patient receipt (PDF) for
the relevant purpose and event.

00:11:24.975 --> 00:11:29.825
A grant, a change and a withdrawal can
have different receipts.

00:11:29.825 --> 00:11:34.335
Check that you selected the correct row
before handing over a copy.

00:11:34.335 --> 00:11:39.560
Store downloaded documents securely;
authorised access to a download is not

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:42.821
permission to leave it on a shared
desktop.

00:11:43.568 --> 00:11:49.868
The PDF shows Your recorded choice,
Purpose, Recorded on, notice information

00:11:49.868 --> 00:11:52.153
and a receipt reference.

00:11:52.153 --> 00:11:56.103
Patient name is labelled as the current
hospital record.

00:11:56.103 --> 00:11:59.788
The notice language belongs to the
recorded event.

00:11:59.788 --> 00:12:04.983
Read Check the latest status: a historical
grant does not guarantee that permission

00:12:04.983 --> 00:12:06.788
is active now.

00:12:06.788 --> 00:12:11.953
The QR opens a status check; the printable
summary is not itself a newly signed

00:12:11.953 --> 00:12:14.254
clinical consent form.

00:12:14.985 --> 00:12:21.825
Technical verification details contains
Download verification data (JSON) and Copy

00:12:21.825 --> 00:12:24.645
signed token for audit tools.

00:12:24.645 --> 00:12:30.820
Export consent data (JSON) is a separate
profile export containing personal

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:32.590
information.

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:38.390
For a public check, open Check a receipt,
paste the signed token or use Scan QR

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:41.765
image, then choose Check receipt.

00:12:41.765 --> 00:12:47.265
Valid signature describes cryptographic
verification; also read withdrawal,

00:12:47.265 --> 00:12:52.160
superseded and key-status information
before interpreting the result.

00:12:52.902 --> 00:12:57.537
Open Patient consent profile and locate
the active purpose the patient wants to

00:12:57.537 --> 00:12:59.062
withdraw.

00:12:59.062 --> 00:13:01.487
Choose its Withdraw button.

00:13:01.487 --> 00:13:07.037
In Withdraw consent, verify that both the
patient and purpose are correct.

00:13:07.037 --> 00:13:12.717
Enter the Identity verification / request
reference according to hospital procedure,

00:13:12.717 --> 00:13:15.382
then choose Confirm withdrawal.

00:13:15.382 --> 00:13:19.647
This is a selective action: withdrawing
insurance permission does not

00:13:19.647 --> 00:13:22.937
automatically withdraw every other
purpose.

00:13:23.652 --> 00:13:28.007
Wait for the withdrawal confirmation, then
check that the intended purpose is

00:13:28.007 --> 00:13:32.142
Withdrawn while unrelated choices remain
as expected.

00:13:32.142 --> 00:13:36.132
A new withdrawal receipt should appear in
the receipt history.

00:13:36.132 --> 00:13:40.502
The message also explains that downstream
enforcement and legal retention need

00:13:40.502 --> 00:13:41.952
review.

00:13:41.952 --> 00:13:47.042
Do not promise that a laboratory, insurer
or other system has stopped processing

00:13:47.042 --> 00:13:50.998
just because the local status changed
successfully.

00:13:51.735 --> 00:13:55.475
Select Patient directory or Consent
register.

00:13:55.475 --> 00:14:00.040
Use Find patient by name or hospital
number, enter the training name or

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:03.590
hospital number, then choose Search.

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:07.145
Previous and Next move through result
pages.

00:14:07.145 --> 00:14:11.175
Open the matching patient only after
checking identity.

00:14:11.175 --> 00:14:16.800
In Patient consent profile, review the
masked contact, notice language, purpose

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:19.275
statuses and history.

00:14:19.275 --> 00:14:23.530
Similar names are not enough to establish
the correct patient.

00:14:24.277 --> 00:14:29.047
An account may be unable to find or open a
patient because the record is outside its

00:14:29.047 --> 00:14:32.357
hospital, branch or assignment.

00:14:32.357 --> 00:14:37.402
Treat that denial as an access boundary,
not a browser fault.

00:14:37.402 --> 00:14:42.327
Patient linking and staff assignments
require hospital-controlled provisioning;

00:14:42.327 --> 00:14:46.337
this interface has no general Assign
patient button.

00:14:46.337 --> 00:14:50.307
Ask the authorised team to review the
relationship.

00:14:50.307 --> 00:14:53.703
Never ask another person to share their
session.

00:14:54.443 --> 00:14:58.403
Open Data sharing and choose Record
sharing approval.

00:14:58.403 --> 00:15:01.383
Find and select the correct patient.

00:15:01.383 --> 00:15:06.628
Enter Recipient organisation, choose
Purpose and Minimum data category, and

00:15:06.628 --> 00:15:10.783
record Recipient-specific patient approval
evidence.

00:15:10.783 --> 00:15:15.263
Review the expiry explanation, then use
Save record.

00:15:15.263 --> 00:15:20.473
This register records an approval; it does
not transmit reports.

00:15:20.473 --> 00:15:24.878
A general registration OTP does not
authorise disclosure to whichever

00:15:24.878 --> 00:15:28.369
recipient happens to request the
information.

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:33.700
A clinician with the appropriate patient
scope opens Procedure records and chooses

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.255
Record procedure evidence.

00:15:36.255 --> 00:15:41.520
Select the patient, enter Procedure and
Responsible clinician, then add the Signed

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:45.160
clinical consent and witness evidence
reference.

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:49.055
Use Save record after reviewing the source
document.

00:15:49.055 --> 00:15:51.870
This action stores a reference.

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:56.610
It does not create a patient signature,
witness signature or clinically adequate

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:59.191
consent document on its own.

00:15:59.902 --> 00:16:05.162
For a child, check the date of birth and
the Guardian for consent section.

00:16:05.162 --> 00:16:08.622
Use Add verified guardian when
appropriate.

00:16:08.622 --> 00:16:14.122
Record the guardian's identity, date of
birth, relationship and mobile number,

00:16:14.122 --> 00:16:19.257
then choose How identity was verified and
enter Verification reference.

00:16:19.257 --> 00:16:23.252
Confirm the in-person authority
attestation only after the hospital's

00:16:23.252 --> 00:16:25.357
checks are complete.

00:16:25.357 --> 00:16:29.168
Never enter a full Aadhaar number as the
reference.

00:16:29.902 --> 00:16:34.207
The active guardian panel identifies who
is giving consent and which contact

00:16:34.207 --> 00:16:36.182
receives the code.

00:16:36.182 --> 00:16:40.067
Review these details before generating a
challenge.

00:16:40.067 --> 00:16:45.317
The child's purpose options may be
restricted, including marketing.

00:16:45.317 --> 00:16:49.957
Do not bypass those restrictions or assume
the software applies every healthcare

00:16:49.957 --> 00:16:52.307
exemption automatically.

00:16:52.307 --> 00:16:56.792
When the child reaches adulthood, guardian
authority and patient access need the

00:16:56.792 --> 00:17:01.208
hospital's approved handover and
identity-review process.

00:17:01.943 --> 00:17:06.438
For an adult, record a lawful guardian
only where verified legal authority

00:17:06.438 --> 00:17:10.888
applies; disability by itself is not
sufficient.

00:17:10.888 --> 00:17:15.983
The form offers appropriate court-order or
guardianship evidence methods.

00:17:15.983 --> 00:17:20.168
Replace guardian starts a new verified
relationship.

00:17:20.168 --> 00:17:25.148
Revoke guardian requires a reason and
affects future consent collection.

00:17:25.148 --> 00:17:29.533
It does not silently cancel every consent
already given.

00:17:29.533 --> 00:17:34.713
Review the guardian history after either
action and escalate uncertain authority.

00:17:35.443 --> 00:17:41.418
A separately provisioned patient account
opens My privacy and Your privacy choices.

00:17:41.418 --> 00:17:46.453
Your hospital-linked record identifies the
record linked by the hospital.

00:17:46.453 --> 00:17:50.808
This is not a phone-number search or
self-enrolment service.

00:17:50.808 --> 00:17:54.268
Review your purpose statuses and receipts.

00:17:54.268 --> 00:17:59.008
Review or change my choices opens the
notice journey when available; an active

00:17:59.008 --> 00:18:01.908
purpose also offers withdrawal.

00:18:01.908 --> 00:18:05.729
Sign out if the displayed identity is not
yours.

00:18:06.443 --> 00:18:11.028
Under Your data requests, choose Send a
data request.

00:18:11.028 --> 00:18:17.508
Request type offers Access, Correction,
Erasure review, Grievance and Nomination.

00:18:17.508 --> 00:18:22.873
Select the appropriate type, explain What
would you like the hospital to do, then

00:18:22.873 --> 00:18:25.133
choose Send request.

00:18:25.133 --> 00:18:29.273
Use a separate, clear request for a
different issue.

00:18:29.273 --> 00:18:34.863
Submission sends work to the privacy team;
it does not immediately correct a record,

00:18:34.863 --> 00:18:38.449
erase clinical information or approve a
nominee.

00:18:39.193 --> 00:18:43.623
Choose Read request and response to
inspect the hospital's recorded status and

00:18:43.623 --> 00:18:45.663
response target.

00:18:45.663 --> 00:18:49.448
Use Refresh my records to retrieve
updates.

00:18:49.448 --> 00:18:54.513
For an active permission you want to
withdraw, choose Withdraw, review Withdraw

00:18:54.513 --> 00:18:58.108
this permission and confirm with Withdraw
permission.

00:18:58.108 --> 00:19:01.768
Check Action in connected systems
afterwards.

00:19:01.768 --> 00:19:06.158
Delivery acknowledged means the message
was acknowledged, not independently

00:19:06.158 --> 00:19:10.699
verified deletion or proof that every
downstream use stopped.

00:19:11.443 --> 00:19:15.618
Staff can receive requests outside the
patient portal.

00:19:15.618 --> 00:19:19.333
In Patient rights, choose New request.

00:19:19.333 --> 00:19:23.853
Search for and select the verified
patient, choose Request type and enter

00:19:23.853 --> 00:19:26.003
Request details.

00:19:26.003 --> 00:19:31.823
Record Identity verification / request
reference, then Save record.

00:19:31.823 --> 00:19:35.213
The same five request types are available.

00:19:35.213 --> 00:19:40.068
Reception may record the intake, but
privacy-team permission is required to

00:19:40.068 --> 00:19:43.213
fulfil it or make a retention decision.

00:19:43.943 --> 00:19:49.613
Open Patient rights, locate the Access
case and choose Review request.

00:19:49.613 --> 00:19:54.458
Read Request history, identity evidence
and the service target.

00:19:54.458 --> 00:19:59.013
Download data summary creates a protected
export for the authorised response

00:19:59.013 --> 00:20:00.748
process.

00:20:00.748 --> 00:20:06.663
In Fulfil request, enter How the summary
was provided and any Internal notes.

00:20:06.663 --> 00:20:12.418
Select Fulfil request only after providing
the response through the approved channel.

00:20:12.418 --> 00:20:15.958
Reopen the request to review the saved
result.

00:20:15.958 --> 00:20:19.998
A downloaded file alone is not evidence of
delivery.

00:20:20.735 --> 00:20:25.635
For a Correction case, open the request
and verify the requested change against

00:20:25.635 --> 00:20:27.795
hospital evidence.

00:20:27.795 --> 00:20:33.035
Under Corrected values, complete only the
fields that should change; leave the

00:20:33.035 --> 00:20:34.890
others blank.

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:40.840
Review the proposed name, contact, date of
birth or language carefully, then use

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:42.990
Fulfil request.

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:47.825
If more evidence is needed, use Update
status and Awaiting information instead of

00:20:47.825 --> 00:20:49.305
guessing.

00:20:49.305 --> 00:20:52.425
Review the request history after saving.

00:20:53.152 --> 00:20:57.307
Open the Erasure review request and read
the existing patient state and Legal

00:20:57.307 --> 00:20:58.812
holds.

00:20:58.812 --> 00:21:04.012
Under Decision, choose Erase personal data
or Refuse with legal basis only after

00:21:04.012 --> 00:21:07.327
reviewing the applicable records policy.

00:21:07.327 --> 00:21:11.077
If refusing, record the Legal basis.

00:21:11.077 --> 00:21:14.562
Use Fulfil request to apply the decision.

00:21:14.562 --> 00:21:18.687
The system may schedule anonymisation
after required retention instead of

00:21:18.687 --> 00:21:23.722
deleting immediately, and downstream
obligations remain separate.

00:21:24.443 --> 00:21:29.403
In an authorised rights-request detail,
find Legal holds.

00:21:29.403 --> 00:21:34.498
Enter Reason and Legal basis, then choose
Place legal hold when preservation is

00:21:34.498 --> 00:21:36.098
required.

00:21:36.098 --> 00:21:40.308
An active hold prevents applicable erasure
processing.

00:21:40.308 --> 00:21:45.223
Release hold requires an accountable
reason; use it only after the authorised

00:21:45.223 --> 00:21:46.673
review.

00:21:46.673 --> 00:21:50.628
Releasing a hold is not itself an
instruction that every record should now

00:21:50.628 --> 00:21:52.238
be deleted.

00:21:52.238 --> 00:21:56.209
Recheck the request and retention schedule
afterwards.

00:21:56.943 --> 00:22:01.103
Open the Grievance case, read the
patient's concern and check the published

00:22:01.103 --> 00:22:03.138
response target.

00:22:03.138 --> 00:22:08.243
In Fulfil request, enter Response,
retention decision and fulfilment evidence

00:22:08.243 --> 00:22:12.533
with a clear explanation of what was
investigated and decided.

00:22:12.533 --> 00:22:17.453
If the issue is still being investigated,
Update status can record In review or

00:22:17.453 --> 00:22:19.633
Awaiting information.

00:22:19.633 --> 00:22:23.558
Do not label an unresolved complaint
complete just to meet an internal

00:22:23.558 --> 00:22:25.533
dashboard target.

00:22:26.277 --> 00:22:31.702
For Nomination, verify the patient's
instructions and complete Nominee name,

00:22:31.702 --> 00:22:38.427
Relationship, Nominee mobile number and
Identity verification / request reference.

00:22:38.427 --> 00:22:42.262
Use Fulfil request after the required
checks.

00:22:42.262 --> 00:22:45.887
The nominee appears in Nominees with a
status.

00:22:45.887 --> 00:22:49.782
Revoke nomination asks for identity
evidence.

00:22:49.782 --> 00:22:54.612
Naming a nominee does not give that person
an unrestricted staff account or automatic

00:22:54.612 --> 00:22:58.278
access to the patient's entire hospital
record.

00:22:59.027 --> 00:23:03.292
Select Incident response, then Log an
incident.

00:23:03.292 --> 00:23:10.077
Enter Incident title, the actual time the
hospital became aware, and Nature, scope,

00:23:10.077 --> 00:23:12.832
likely impact and containment.

00:23:12.832 --> 00:23:16.722
Check the computer's timezone before
entering time.

00:23:16.722 --> 00:23:22.317
After saving, open Breach workflow and
complete Assessment: nature, extent,

00:23:22.317 --> 00:23:28.697
timing, location, impact, consequences,
mitigation and safety measures.

00:23:28.697 --> 00:23:30.907
Choose Save assessment.

00:23:30.907 --> 00:23:35.737
Do not substitute the time you opened this
screen for earlier awareness.

00:23:36.485 --> 00:23:40.980
Review Initial intimation to the Board and
use Preview message before Send initial

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:42.690
intimation.

00:23:42.690 --> 00:23:48.270
In this training workspace, the notifier
logs a simulated message; it does not

00:23:48.270 --> 00:23:50.290
contact the Board.

00:23:50.290 --> 00:23:55.395
Add the Hospital numbers of affected
patients using Add affected patients.

00:23:55.395 --> 00:24:00.765
Review the affected list and patient
notice preview before Notify patients.

00:24:00.765 --> 00:24:04.900
Failed or unreachable notices need
follow-up, not an assumption that

00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:06.975
everybody was told.

00:24:07.693 --> 00:24:12.123
Open Detailed report to the Board and
complete the updated description, relevant

00:24:12.123 --> 00:24:16.793
facts, mitigation, findings and remedial
measures.

00:24:16.793 --> 00:24:21.193
Check the assessment and patient-notice
information before choosing Send detailed

00:24:21.193 --> 00:24:23.438
report and confirming.

00:24:23.438 --> 00:24:27.178
This training action records a simulated
report.

00:24:27.178 --> 00:24:32.328
The seventy-two-hour deadline concerns the
detailed report; initial intimation is

00:24:32.328 --> 00:24:34.048
without delay.

00:24:34.048 --> 00:24:39.543
CERT-In reporting is a separate process,
not completed by this screen.

00:24:40.277 --> 00:24:45.572
Before closing a report, Board extension
can record an extension already granted in

00:24:45.572 --> 00:24:46.967
writing.

00:24:46.967 --> 00:24:52.187
Enter Extended deadline and Board
reference, then Record extension.

00:24:52.187 --> 00:24:57.382
To document communication outside this
app, select Record evidence of intimations

00:24:57.382 --> 00:24:59.732
made outside the system.

00:24:59.732 --> 00:25:03.717
Enter the Board references and
affected-person evidence, then Save

00:25:03.717 --> 00:25:05.127
record.

00:25:05.127 --> 00:25:09.077
Use clearly labelled synthetic references
in training.

00:25:09.077 --> 00:25:13.483
Never invent a regulator approval or a
delivery confirmation.

00:25:14.193 --> 00:25:19.968
In Readiness & settings, find Retention
and erasure and choose Add policy.

00:25:19.968 --> 00:25:26.483
Enter Policy name, Applies to, Retention
period, Notice before erasure and Legal or

00:25:26.483 --> 00:25:28.543
records basis.

00:25:28.543 --> 00:25:32.193
Policy is active controls whether it runs.

00:25:32.193 --> 00:25:36.378
Save policy only after hospital records
review.

00:25:36.378 --> 00:25:40.703
The demo's minimums and inactivity
workflow are not universal medical-record

00:25:40.703 --> 00:25:46.968
retention advice, and statutory holds or
other required retention still apply.

00:25:47.693 --> 00:25:53.858
Review Scheduled erasures, Erasure notices
and Recent runs before using Run now.

00:25:53.858 --> 00:26:00.123
That action can carry out due erasures;
practise only on the synthetic exercise.

00:26:00.123 --> 00:26:05.088
Cancel erasure asks why the schedule
should stop, such as verified patient

00:26:05.088 --> 00:26:06.768
contact.

00:26:06.768 --> 00:26:11.218
A hold or patient-contact change can
affect eligibility.

00:26:11.218 --> 00:26:17.623
After a run, inspect notified, failed,
held and cancelled counts, remembering

00:26:17.623 --> 00:26:21.033
that a logged notice is not handset
delivery.

00:26:21.777 --> 00:26:26.662
A privacy author opens Readiness &
settings, then Notice publication and

00:26:26.662 --> 00:26:28.922
Create notice version.

00:26:28.922 --> 00:26:35.642
Enter Version reference, Patient notice
language, title, hospital privacy contact,

00:26:35.642 --> 00:26:39.157
full text and confirmation statement.

00:26:39.157 --> 00:26:44.997
Complete the withdrawal, rights, grievance
and complaint information URLs.

00:26:44.997 --> 00:26:50.322
Select only the consent purposes being
published and enter their names, data,

00:26:50.322 --> 00:26:52.782
uses and categories.

00:26:52.782 --> 00:26:57.207
Create the version, then expand it and
Submit for review.

00:26:57.943 --> 00:27:01.933
Sign in as a different authorised privacy
reviewer.

00:27:01.933 --> 00:27:06.858
Expand the In review version and read the
complete content, purpose definitions and

00:27:06.858 --> 00:27:09.338
communication channels.

00:27:09.338 --> 00:27:14.218
Enter Legal review reference and Language
and audio review reference; where audio

00:27:14.218 --> 00:27:18.258
metadata exists, review its reference too.

00:27:18.258 --> 00:27:23.188
Tick the independent-review attestation
only after checking the actual evidence,

00:27:23.188 --> 00:27:26.038
then choose Approve reviewed version.

00:27:26.038 --> 00:27:29.158
The author cannot approve their own
document.

00:27:29.902 --> 00:27:34.667
An authorised hospital administrator opens
the Approved version and selects Publish

00:27:34.667 --> 00:27:35.892
now.

00:27:35.892 --> 00:27:40.532
Publication is for that exact hospital and
language; it does not give the

00:27:40.532 --> 00:27:43.677
administrator patient-read access.

00:27:43.677 --> 00:27:47.072
Changes require a new version and review.

00:27:47.072 --> 00:27:51.832
To retire an effective version, enter
Reason for retirement and choose Retire

00:27:51.832 --> 00:27:53.292
version.

00:27:53.292 --> 00:27:57.917
If no replacement exists, consent
collection in that language becomes

00:27:57.917 --> 00:28:02.272
unavailable rather than silently reverting
to an older notice.

00:28:02.985 --> 00:28:08.195
Platform administration can use Add
hospital to create a hospital identifier,

00:28:08.195 --> 00:28:11.785
name, short code and first branch.

00:28:11.785 --> 00:28:16.480
A hospital administrator operates within
the selected hospital under Hospitals and

00:28:16.480 --> 00:28:18.110
accounts.

00:28:18.110 --> 00:28:22.640
Add branch accepts a branch identifier and
Branch name.

00:28:22.640 --> 00:28:25.795
Verify the hospital before saving.

00:28:25.795 --> 00:28:29.820
Activate and Deactivate change
availability; they do not remove

00:28:29.820 --> 00:28:34.651
historical records or transfer patient
data to another hospital.

00:28:35.402 --> 00:28:41.522
Under Accounts, use Add account and enter
Email, Role, Branch and Temporary password

00:28:41.522 --> 00:28:43.747
for a synthetic learner.

00:28:43.747 --> 00:28:46.667
Choose the least permission required.

00:28:46.667 --> 00:28:53.432
Existing accounts offer role Save, Set
password, Unlock, Reset authenticator,

00:28:53.432 --> 00:28:55.887
Activate and Deactivate.

00:28:55.887 --> 00:29:00.567
Investigate the requester's identity
before credential actions.

00:29:00.567 --> 00:29:05.097
There is no patient-assignment editor
here: creating a patient-role account

00:29:05.097 --> 00:29:08.342
alone does not link it to a patient
record.

00:29:09.068 --> 00:29:14.698
Authenticator policy lets an administrator
select a Role, set Require authenticator

00:29:14.698 --> 00:29:16.578
and choose Save.

00:29:16.578 --> 00:29:21.493
Plan enrolment and recovery support before
enforcing a requirement.

00:29:21.493 --> 00:29:25.723
Notice delivery lists queued or attempted
notifications with their provider and

00:29:25.723 --> 00:29:27.328
status.

00:29:27.328 --> 00:29:32.308
A log provider is simulation, not an SMS
receipt.

00:29:32.308 --> 00:29:37.608
Administrative resets and policy changes
belong in the access review; they do not

00:29:37.608 --> 00:29:42.968
establish that the hospital has completed
production identity qualification.

00:29:43.693 --> 00:29:47.888
Receipt signing keys is a separate
administrator control.

00:29:47.888 --> 00:29:51.533
Read the listed key states and Public keys
link.

00:29:51.533 --> 00:29:55.933
Only an approved key operator should use
Rotate signing key.

00:29:55.933 --> 00:30:01.293
Rotation retires the previous key; Revoke
accepts a retired key and requires a

00:30:01.293 --> 00:30:02.713
Reason.

00:30:02.713 --> 00:30:06.523
Revocation changes verification outcomes.

00:30:06.523 --> 00:30:11.268
Practise only in the disposable training
hospital, following the key-management

00:30:11.268 --> 00:30:16.368
runbook, and never treat rotation as a
routine reception task.

00:30:17.110 --> 00:30:21.620
An auditor opens Audit trail to inspect
actions within their authorised hospital

00:30:21.620 --> 00:30:23.095
scope.

00:30:23.095 --> 00:30:28.165
Review Actor, time and record references,
then choose Inspect evidence for the

00:30:28.165 --> 00:30:30.010
relevant event.

00:30:30.010 --> 00:30:33.890
Read what the event actually records
instead of assuming it proves every

00:30:33.890 --> 00:30:36.015
external outcome.

00:30:36.015 --> 00:30:40.255
Auditors do not receive general
patient-directory or edit access merely

00:30:40.255 --> 00:30:43.435
because they can inspect audit evidence.

00:30:43.435 --> 00:30:47.416
Handle exported or displayed evidence as
confidential.

00:30:48.152 --> 00:30:53.087
Choose Verify local chain and read the
result and number of events checked.

00:30:53.087 --> 00:30:58.402
A successful result means the available
local chain is internally consistent.

00:30:58.402 --> 00:31:02.722
It does not independently protect against
every privileged database rewrite or

00:31:02.722 --> 00:31:04.487
missing tail.

00:31:04.487 --> 00:31:08.382
Independent signed checkpoints and
separately controlled storage remain

00:31:08.382 --> 00:31:10.372
production work.

00:31:10.372 --> 00:31:15.317
Preserve evidence and escalate a failed
check; do not delete or recreate records

00:31:15.317 --> 00:31:17.847
to make the result turn green.

00:31:18.568 --> 00:31:24.298
In Readiness & settings, inspect Consent
propagation webhooks, Subscribers and

00:31:24.298 --> 00:31:26.013
Deliveries.

00:31:26.013 --> 00:31:30.903
Delivery status filters pending, delivered
and dead-letter work.

00:31:30.903 --> 00:31:35.893
Approved non-public environments can
expose Add subscriber, Dispatch now and

00:31:35.893 --> 00:31:41.143
Retry; the public synthetic demo disables
outbound webhooks.

00:31:41.143 --> 00:31:45.653
Do not demonstrate a real receiver or
reveal a signing secret.

00:31:45.653 --> 00:31:51.483
Delivered describes transport, not proof
that the recipient stopped using data.

00:31:52.193 --> 00:31:56.153
The processor register and signed
processing-acknowledgement module is

00:31:56.153 --> 00:32:01.153
operated through technical APIs, not a
front-desk screen.

00:32:01.153 --> 00:32:06.248
Hospital IT binds contracted processors
and tests authenticated callbacks for

00:32:06.248 --> 00:32:08.843
exact consent revisions.

00:32:08.843 --> 00:32:13.198
A receiver-attested result is that
receiver's statement, not independent

00:32:13.198 --> 00:32:15.088
verification.

00:32:15.088 --> 00:32:19.928
Older acknowledgements cannot establish
the current withdrawal outcome.

00:32:19.928 --> 00:32:24.983
Ask the integration owner for the relevant
evidence and unresolved actions; do not

00:32:24.983 --> 00:32:28.139
look for a nonexistent processor button.

00:32:28.860 --> 00:32:34.215
The managed edge feature buffers prepared
staff-assisted withdrawal intents only.

00:32:34.215 --> 00:32:39.285
It needs a qualified local node and an
online, short-lived capability prepared

00:32:39.285 --> 00:32:41.000
beforehand.

00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:47.395
Hospital IT operates its APIs; this GUI
has no offline capture switch.

00:32:47.395 --> 00:32:51.575
A locally buffered intent is not yet a
central withdrawal.

00:32:51.575 --> 00:32:56.575
Stale revisions, revoked access, full
storage or missing tickets require

00:32:56.575 --> 00:33:02.320
reconciliation or the approved downtime
process, never automatic offline grants or

00:33:02.320 --> 00:33:04.880
expired OTP replay.

00:33:05.610 --> 00:33:11.975
A patient may have no private phone, share
a family phone, be unable to read, or need

00:33:11.975 --> 00:33:14.005
emergency care.

00:33:14.005 --> 00:33:19.210
Do not invent contact details, reuse
another patient's code or assume a shared

00:33:19.210 --> 00:33:22.090
number permits portal access.

00:33:22.090 --> 00:33:26.520
This build does not complete every
alternative-signature or emergency-capture

00:33:26.520 --> 00:33:28.130
workflow.

00:33:28.130 --> 00:33:32.760
Use the hospital-approved assisted,
clinical or paper route and document the

00:33:32.760 --> 00:33:34.405
follow-up.

00:33:34.405 --> 00:33:39.460
Emergency treatment must not wait for an
OTP or portal completion.

00:33:40.193 --> 00:33:44.303
Internet loss differs from loss of the
hospital server.

00:33:44.303 --> 00:33:49.273
A healthy local server may remain
available on the LAN, while SMS or cloud

00:33:49.273 --> 00:33:51.253
services fail.

00:33:51.253 --> 00:33:55.873
If the server is unreachable, an ordinary
browser save is not automatically

00:33:55.873 --> 00:33:57.343
buffered.

00:33:57.343 --> 00:34:01.888
Check the displayed error, preserve only
approved references and use the agreed

00:34:01.888 --> 00:34:04.153
downtime procedure.

00:34:04.153 --> 00:34:08.463
Do not repeatedly create records or claim
a save succeeded without a durable

00:34:08.463 --> 00:34:10.168
acknowledgement.

00:34:10.902 --> 00:34:17.227
Before finishing, review overdue requests,
unresolved delivery failures, withdrawn

00:34:17.227 --> 00:34:22.247
purposes needing follow-up and any
scheduled erasures or open incidents.

00:34:22.247 --> 00:34:26.642
Hand over responsibilities and evidence
references through the hospital's approved

00:34:26.642 --> 00:34:28.087
channel.

00:34:28.087 --> 00:34:33.367
Secure patient PDFs and exports, clear
shared-device documents according to

00:34:33.367 --> 00:34:36.187
policy and select Sign out.

00:34:36.187 --> 00:34:39.697
Do not leave an account open for the next
shift.

00:34:39.697 --> 00:34:44.708
Return to the relevant chapter whenever a
workflow or permission is uncertain.
